\begin{abstract}
A search for radio recombination lines near 20 cm at z=0.193 and z=0.886
towards the gravitational lens system PKS 1830-211 has yielded upper
limits of $|\tau_L| \leq$~5 $\times$ 10$^{-5}$~and $\leq$~5 $\times$ 
10$^{-4}$~ at the two redshifts respectively. Based on the 
non-detections, we derive upper
limits to the emission measure of the ionized gas in the absorbing
systems. We also present continuum flux density measurements over the
frequency range 0.3$-$45 GHz made at a single epoch.
\end{abstract}

